 @fireguy615  2 years now with the R27U81-A (China model of a TCL HVA panel). My particular model did unfortunately run into intermittent low frequency VRR flicker issues when local dimming is enabled, its not horrific but it is noticeable under certain conditions. Even with this problem, I would still gladly take the general weaknesses of MiniLED HVA over the shortfalls of OLED, and the abysmal contrast from my previous 1440p IPS monitor drove me insane during any sort of dark scene content or UI so im not even sure I would want to go for MiniLED IPS either.

You really have to assess how much perfect HDR EOTF curve tracking and nearly non-existent low latency on OLEDs matter to you when compared to the text fringing, babysitting the burn-in, overall weaker bright room handling that you dont have to deal with in MiniLED. Im of the opinion OLED monitors, even with the recent improvements, still make the most sense for people who are willing to treat them like a TV, you turn it on for your movies and gaming, and then turn them off when you are done.

For me to be willing to switch to OLED in the eventual future, I would need to see burn warranties bumped from 3yr-->5yr (long enough to have upgraded the GPU, and for non-HDR related monitor tech to have incremented), the text fringing to be entirely resolved, and fullscreen nits to be 400-500+ to render bright rooms a non-issue.
